exemplar.en:
Corrected HTML snippet:
```html
<nav aria-label="Primary">
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
    <li><a href="/product">Product</a></li>
    <li><a href="/docs" aria-current="page">Docs</a></li>
    <li><a href="/pricing">Pricing</a></li>
    <li><a href="/about">About</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>
```
Corrected helper code:
```ts
export type RouteRecord = {
  id: string;
  path: string;
};

function normalizePath(value: string): string {
  const trimmed = value.trim().toLowerCase();
  if (trimmed === "/") return "/";
  return trimmed.replace(/\/+$/, "");
}

export function getCurrentPageId(pathname: string, routes: RouteRecord[]): string {
  const normalizedPathname = normalizePath(pathname);
  const matches = routes.filter((route) => normalizePath(route.path) === normalizedPathname);
  if (matches.length === 1) return matches[0].id;
  if (matches.length > 1) return "ambiguous";
  return "not-found";
}
```
Test cases and expected outputs:
- getCurrentPageId("/", routes) === "home"
- getCurrentPageId("/Docs/", routes) === "docs"
- getCurrentPageId("/PRODUCT", routes) === "product"
- getCurrentPageId("/pricing/", routes) === "pricing"
- getCurrentPageId("/missing/", routes) === "not-found"

Decisions: replaced Docs span with anchor, moved aria-current to Docs only, replaced Pricing button with anchor. Normalized both pathname and route.path by trim, lowercase, and removing trailing slashes except root. Limitations: no browser executed, only supplied routes. Owner: Ada Wong, frontend team lead.

