exemplar.en:
Fictional simulation, not endorsed by Oursky. The shipped mapper fails R3 and R4: it trims the optional displayName directly, so u-03 and u-05 (absent displayName per R5) throw a TypeError, and u-02 (whitespace only) silently returns '' instead of the trimmed legacyName. Corrected function:
```ts
export function toNewProfile(record: LegacyRecord): NewProfile {
  const fromDisplay = (record.displayName ?? '').trim();
  const fromLegacy = (record.legacyName ?? '').trim();
  const displayName = fromDisplay !== '' ? fromDisplay : fromLegacy !== '' ? fromLegacy : 'anonymous';
  return { id: record.id, displayName };
}
```
Evidence and tests: u-01 gives 'Mei Lam', u-02 gives 'Chan Tai Man', u-03 gives 'Wong Ka Yee', u-04 gives 'Ada', u-05 gives 'anonymous'. Add a boundary case of absent displayName and whitespace-only legacyName expecting 'anonymous', and assert the input record is not mutated and no call throws. Limitations: the throw findings are a static reading of the shown code, no runtime was executed, and no database or SQL migration is in scope. Next step: reviewer confirms the patch and adds u-02 and u-05 as regression tests. Owner: fictional team lead Cheryl Ho.

exemplar.zh:
